If you kick/break a door, it's not really gone, though... if you stand
on the square where the door used to be, and look down with ":" it
tells you "There is a broken door here."  Plus, zapping a wand of
locking at the spot where the door was gives you "The broken door
reassembles and locks!" (or "A cloud of dust springs up and assembles
itself into a door!" if you break the door with e.g. a bolt of cold).

In fact (as I just wiztested), the pit + boulder method doesn't prevent
the (re)creation of a door either.  In double fact, it appears that if
you dig a gap in a wall, the game treats it as a doorway, and any
doorway can sport a door if you zap it with a wand of locking.  Handy
stuff! unless you hate doors as much as I do...

